From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix narrow-string conversion in 7zUpdate.cpp IsExeFile

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [p7zip 16.02 (SourceForge) is unmaintained upstream; this file's
#ifndef _WIN32 IsExeFile() passes a UString directly to CInFile::Open(), which only accepts
CFSTR (the filesystem-string type: narrow AString when USE_UNICODE_FSTRING is unset). This
mismatch is latent in every p7zip 16.02 Linux/macOS build, exposed here as a hard
"no matching function" error rather than a pre-C++11 implicit-conversion warning, same as the
Debian 15-Fix-FTBFS-gcc10.patch class of fix this port already carries upstream's own patch
for. us2fs() is the project's own macro for this exact conversion (identity when FString is
already wide, a real AString conversion otherwise) and is already used the same way a few
lines up in CPP/7zip/UI/Common/Bench.cpp.]

--- a/CPP/7zip/Archive/7z/7zUpdate.cpp
+++ b/CPP/7zip/Archive/7z/7zUpdate.cpp
@@ -814,7 +814,7 @@ static bool IsExeFile(const CUpdateItem &ui)
       // file has the execution flag and it's big enought
       // try to find if the file is a script
       NWindows::NFile::NIO::CInFile file;
-      if (file.Open(ui.Name))
+      if (file.Open(us2fs(ui.Name)))
       {
         char buffer[2048];
         UINT32 processedSize;
